PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C}

The relevant Ontario ESA rules (as amended) require a written disconnect-from-work policy for any employer with 25+ employees on January 1 of a given year; the policy must be prepared by March 1 and a copy given to every employee (including new hires) within 30 days of preparation or any update. An electronic-monitoring policy carries the identical threshold and distribution rules, but its first compliance deadline is March 1 2023.  

- A, B, D and E all have fewer than 25 employees on the January 1 dates that matter, so they are exempt from both policies.  
- C has ~1 000 employees on every relevant January 1 and therefore must maintain both policies and meet the 30-day distribution rule after every update. Updating monthly but distributing only quarterly necessarily exceeds the 30-day window on multiple occasions, rendering C non-compliant on 2 January 2023.  

Thus C is the only employer that violates the statute.}

